00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.890
China has backed itself into a corner.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:30.859
About a year ago, in Spring 2020, it emerged
triumphant—after months of devastation,

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:38.300
it became the first country to coax life back
to near-normal after a widespread COVID epidemic.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.870
Just as it emerged from lockdown, the rest
of the world was entering into it, so China

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.920
started to focus its attention on not only
recovering from COVID, but also from the hit

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.650
it took to its global image as a result of
perceived mismanagement in the virus’ early

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.650
days.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:59.170
As the US and Europe struggled from far larger,
far more devastating outbreaks, China sat

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:03.830
on the sidelines, working on ways to be viewed
not only as the country that crushed COVID

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.100
within its borders, but also led the fight
against it around the world.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.280
They wanted to be seen doing what the US and
Europe couldn’t while they were focused

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.220
on their problems at home.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.190
As hospital ships docked and intensive care
units ballooned in size throughout April in

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:23.450
New York, planes were landing at JFK carrying
thousands of desperately-needed ventilators

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.600
from China.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.670
As hospitals around the world ran out of supplies
and required healthcare workers to reuse masks

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:35.020
for days or weeks on end, national airlines
were making special, dedicated trips to pick

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.600
up medical supplies donated by China.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.530
As every corner in the world worked to ramp
up testing to get a more accurate picture

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:46.770
of their problems, Chinese-made test kits
were streaming through their borders.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:52.210
China was at the center of the fight against
the virus, but the center can be the riskiest

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.970
place to be.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:02:00.160
As donations turned into purchases, it emerged
that there was a major quality problem.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:05.400
Some 90% of mask certifications from China,
according to one measure, were fake; tests

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.889
that were supposed to have 80% sensitivity
actually had 30%; and stories emerged globally

00:02:10.889 --> 00:02:15.859
of Chinese officials demanding public displays
of thanks in exchange for donations.

00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:22.120
What was supposed to be a diplomacy coup rekindled
an old narrative of Chinese-made as inferior.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:28.099
At best, this effort did little to rewrite
China’s role in the pandemic, but at worst,

00:02:28.099 --> 00:02:33.290
it seems very possible that it actually further
damaged their global image.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:38.340
However, while the start and the middle of
the pandemic did not entirely go China’s

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:43.519
way, in terms of global image, there was still
the end.

00:02:43.519 --> 00:02:48.480
China still had the chance to recover what
they’d lost and, more specifically, they

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:54.249
had the chance to display their home-grown
scientific skill and manufacturing might.

00:02:54.249 --> 00:02:57.980
China could be the country that supplies the
shots that would end the world’s misery

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.519
and put the pandemic in the history books.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:07.689
They could make the world’s vaccine, but,
of course, first, they needed a vaccine.

00:03:07.689 --> 00:03:10.079
Luckily, they had a head-start.

00:03:10.079 --> 00:03:15.000
As soon as the outbreak begun in China, a
number of private companies, state-owned enterprises,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.980
and government-run institutes started work
on developing a vaccine.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:24.980
By Spring, there were some strong, viable
candidates, so the next step was testing.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:31.389
Just as most of the western world entered
their lockdowns, the first Chinese vaccine—Ad5-nCoV

00:03:31.389 --> 00:03:38.499
by CanSino Biologics—entered a Phase I clinical
trial on March 17th, 2020, with 108 adults

00:03:38.499 --> 00:03:40.889
in Wuhan receiving the shot.

00:03:40.889 --> 00:03:46.430
After positive data, this same vaccine became
the first in the world to enter Phase II trials

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:49.909
on April 11th, with 508 participants.

00:03:49.909 --> 00:03:54.150
When the results from that trial were published
on July 20th, they revealed that not only

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.510
was the vaccine acceptably safe, but that
it was also generating the desired immune

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:03.230
response—in short, it was seemingly both
safe and effective.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:08.480
However, the next phase of clinical testing
presented a problem for CanSino.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:14.409
You see, Phase I vaccine trials are about
seeing if they're safe, and then phase II

00:04:14.409 --> 00:04:18.849
trials are about seeing if they generate the
desired immune response in the body.

00:04:18.849 --> 00:04:24.490
Phase III, however, that’s about seeing
if a vaccine works in the real world—to

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.650
see if it actually protects humans.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:33.280
To do so, researchers divide the study participants
into two equal-sized groups.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:38.740
One receives the actual candidate vaccine,
the other receives a placebo shot—typically

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.150
just a saline solution.

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:45.110
Then, the two groups are tracked to see if
one is less likely to contract the virus than

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.110
the other.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:50.460
The problem for CanSino, the other Chinese
vaccine makers, and the country at a whole

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:56.130
was that, by late-summer, when the first Chinese
vaccines were moving into Phase III trials,

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:00.660
daily COVID cases in the country had been
reduced to double-digit levels in a country

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.460
of well over a billion.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:09.080
Most Phase III vaccine trials have below 50,000
participants, so it would take years, if not

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.639
decades, at those case loads to get to the
hundreds of infections needed in a trial to

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:16.070
prove a vaccine’s efficacy.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:20.229
Essentially, it was impossible for Chinese
companies to complete their COVID vaccines

00:05:20.229 --> 00:05:25.560
in China exactly because the country had done
so well at surprising the virus.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:29.659
Therefore, they had to move abroad.

00:05:29.659 --> 00:05:36.539
The CanSino Ad5-nCoV vaccine started Phase
III trials in Russia, Pakistan, Saudi Arabia,

00:05:36.539 --> 00:05:40.979
Mexico, Argentina, and Chile, while the other
leading candidates moved to dozens of other

00:05:40.979 --> 00:05:44.250
countries with more severe COVID epidemics.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:49.939
However, with many of these, China and its
pharmaceutical companies had to curry favor

00:05:49.939 --> 00:05:51.590
with each government.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:56.020
Typically, that took the form of offering
priority access to the very vaccines that

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.650
they were testing, which was fine… for the
moment.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:03.979
As of now, five Chinese-made vaccines have
been approved in the country.

00:06:03.979 --> 00:06:09.689
In general, there has been widespread criticism
of the country’s vaccine development practices—they’ve

00:06:09.689 --> 00:06:13.530
started vaccinating the general public before
their Phase III trials reached their endpoints,

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.340
they haven't been forthcoming with clinical
trial data, they’ve misrepresented efficacy

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.879
ratings from trials, and more—however, despite
that, there is evidence that these vaccines

00:06:22.879 --> 00:06:28.910
are acceptably safe and effective—even if
potentially less so than other approved vaccines.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:36.310
On December 30th, the BBIBP-CorV vaccine manufactured
by Sinopharm—a Chinese state-owned enterprise—was

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.610
approved in the country, making it one of
the first COVID vaccines in the world to be

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.280
deployed in the general population.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.930
Despite the fact that this vaccine was developed
and manufactured by a company owned by the

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:51.300
Chinese government, and despite the fact that
the country had some 1.4 billion people to

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:58.389
inoculate, many of the first doses of the
Sinopharm vaccine were sent beyond their borders.

00:06:58.389 --> 00:07:02.930
Chinese state-owned media reports that the
company has orders for its vaccine from over

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:07.259
100 countries, although the details of such
orders are not publicly known, leading to

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:10.070
some skepticism over the numbers.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:14.710
We do know details for certain orders, though,
and in some cases, we might know more than

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.639
China wants us to.

00:07:16.639 --> 00:07:20.980
In general, though, China’s goal with its
global vaccine distribution is essentially

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:27.060
to do what it failed to do with masks, ventilators,
and tests in 2020—China wants to be the

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.940
country that ended other country’s epidemics.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:36.930
Now, even though Western vaccines from Moderna
and Pfizer have a 95% efficacy rating compared

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:43.380
to 50% to 83% in Chinese vaccines, those Western
vaccines have order obligations taking up

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.379
their inventory until well into 2022.

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:51.580
However, that's not the case with certain
Chinese vaccines, so some countries are making

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:57.590
the calculation that it's better to have less-effective
vaccines sooner than the alternative.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:04.219
Of course, for China, this is a major diplomacy
coup—countries historically allied with

00:08:04.219 --> 00:08:08.590
the West, such as Hungary and Mexico, are
turning to China.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:13.930
In their narrative, China is doing what the
West cannot.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.289
Of course they want this to continue, and
even ramp up.

00:08:17.289 --> 00:08:22.440
That’s why they’ve been sending their
vaccines all around the world, for free.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:27.990
Mongolia and Sri Lanka received 300,000 doses
of the Sinopharm vaccine; Algeria, Sierra

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:32.870
Leone, and Zimbabwe—200,000; and Belarus,
Equatorial Guinea, Gabon, Mozambique, Namibia,

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:33.870
and Bolivia—100,000.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:40.430
Now, a couple hundred thousand doses isn’t
going to end any of these country’s epidemics,

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:44.640
but it’s enough for clips of healthcare
workers receiving Chinese-made and donated

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.150
vaccinations to make the evening news.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:51.350
It’s also enough for each of these countries
to see that these vaccines are acceptably

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:56.350
safe and effective, giving them little reason
to not order more when China is offering them

00:08:56.350 --> 00:09:00.310
months or years before the big Western manufacturers.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:06.890
However, the fact that many of China’s vaccines
are made and distributed by state-owned enterprises

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:12.160
has led many to wonder whether the country
is choosing who gets these life-saving inoculations

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.510
based on diplomatic intentions.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:20.320
It’s leading many to wonder whether who
lives and who dies in this pandemic is starting

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:25.370
to be based on how friendly the country on
a given person’s passport is to the People’s

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.190
Republic of China.

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:30.460
The answer to this question is not hard to
find.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.530
On the read-out of the call between Chinese
State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:39.550
Yi and Algerian Foreign Minister Sabri Boukadoum,
the Chinese official brought up Algeria’s

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:44.660
vote 50 years ago to switch Chinese representation
at the UN from the Republic of China government,

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:49.870
now known as Taiwan, to the People’s Republic
of China, which most now refer to as China.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:55.180
In addition, the Chinese official noted Algeria’s
participation in China’s Belt and Road infrastructure

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:59.640
development initiative, before announcing
the country’s intention to donate 200,000

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:02.720
Sinopharm vaccine doses to Algeria.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:07.890
Elsewhere, in South America, ten of its twelve
countries have vaccinated their populations

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:11.200
with either purchased or donated Chinese vaccines.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:15.710
The only two exceptions are Suriname—the
lowest population country on the continent—and

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:16.710
Paraguay.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:22.150
Now, Paraguay’s absence on the list of countries
to have received Chinese vaccines is not tough

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:26.660
to figure out—it’s because of another
list that they are on.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:33.470
Paraguay is one of just 15 countries worldwide
that recognizes Taiwan as an independent nation—something

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:36.270
that undermines China’s claims of the island.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:41.330
In fact, there is zero overlap between the
list of countries that recognize Taiwan and

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:44.570
those that have received Chinese COVID vaccines.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:50.120
However, the cases of Algeria and Paraguay
simply show China rewarding its allies, and

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.850
ignoring its foes.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:57.310
This is not at all different from how the
US, for example, has operated so far regarding

00:10:57.310 --> 00:11:02.130
COVID vaccine donations—it’s sent them
to strong allies like Mexico and Canada—although,

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:08.320
it’s quite possible that China is going
beyond rewarding its key existing allies,

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:13.340
and using vaccines to try and form new ones.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:17.400
Brazil and the US have gotten along rather
well in recent years, especially over most

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:22.760
of the past four as Brazilian president Jair
Bolsonaro is an open admirer of former US

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.290
president Donald Trump.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:28.190
That meant that Brazil followed the US’
lead in banning the Chinese telecom giant

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:33.300
Huawei from playing a part in building out
their 5G cell network infrastructure—purportedly

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.440
out of security concerns.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:39.640
Therefore, it was a bit of a surprise when
Brazilian communications minister Fábio Faria

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:44.330
took a trip to Beijing in February and met
with Huawei executives.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:49.080
According to Faria, he “took advantage of
the trip to ask for vaccines, which is what

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.030
everyone is clamoring for.”

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:55.730
Soon after, he posted a letter on Twitter
from the Chinese ambassador to Brazil which

00:11:55.730 --> 00:12:00.490
noted the request, reading “during your
visit to China, you expressed the desire to

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:05.380
continue to strengthen cooperation between
our two countries regarding COVID-19 vaccines.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:08.860
I give this matter great importance.”

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:13.260
A few weeks later, the Brazilian government
announced the rules and structure for its

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:19.220
5G auction and, in a change of course, Huawei
was now allowed to participate.

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:24.650
The company, in response to questions about
this, didn’t even directly deny that a tit-for-tat

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.250
deal took place.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:30.720
In a statement, they said that while they
could not directly provide vaccines, they

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:35.840
could facilitate, “communication in an open
and transparent manner in a topic involving

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:37.080
the two governments.”

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:42.410
While there’s no direct evidence of China
trading vaccines for its foreign policy goals,

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:46.740
people are starting to pay more attention
to situations like this, where countries are

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:52.950
opening the door for such an action, and China’s
certainly not closing that door.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:58.370
While its exact details might still be murky,
it is clear that China is engaging in some

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:01.080
form of vaccine diplomacy.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.570
This, however, presents a problem.

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:10.060
You see, one of the main advantages of mRNA
vaccine technology—the kind used in Moderna

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:15.310
and Pfizer’s COVID vaccines—is that its
relatively easy to manufacture.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:20.190
Most other types of vaccines include an attenuated
or dead version of the virus itself, or a

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:25.440
portion of it, but growing and then processing
the virus itself is a time-consuming process

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.360
that is harder to scale.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:32.270
Meanwhile, mRNA vaccines simply include the
genetic instructions for the body to create

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:36.610
a harmless version of the Coronavirus’ spike
protein which can train the immune system

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:38.070
to respond to it.

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:43.990
Done right, that means that mRNA vaccine production
can be faster than that of attenuated or inactivated

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:49.360
virus, protein-based, or viral vector vaccines—the
technologies that China's vaccines are based

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.360
on.

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:56.680
That means that, after a slow-to-scale manufacturing
processes, priority order obligations to trial-hosting

00:13:56.680 --> 00:14:02.320
countries, a robust program of vaccine diplomacy,
and an insistence to only use Chinese-made

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:07.420
vaccines, that doesn’t leave a whole lot
of Chinese COVID vaccines for China to use

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.130
for itself.

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:15.310
As of March, 2021, China has administered
about 5 doses for every 100 citizens.

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:21.400
That’s compared to between 10 and 15 for
every 100 in most EU countries, 35 for 100

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.880
in the US, and 42 for 100 in the UK.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:29.720
Of course, with very few COVID cases within
its borders, there is less of a pressing need

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:35.480
for vaccination in China, but the country’s
entire foreign image goal during the pandemic

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:40.840
has been to be viewed as better than Europe
or the US—it's to be viewed as the country

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:47.480
that, thanks to its remarkable economic transformation
over the past decades, has caught up to Europe

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:50.240
or the US’ superpower status.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:54.550
At present, estimates believe that China will
attain widespread vaccination towards the

00:14:54.550 --> 00:15:02.810
end of 2022—roughly the same time period
as India, Iran, Egypt, Ethiopia, or Columbia.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:08.090
By that time, assuming all goes to plan, most
of the Western World will have been back to

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:13.930
normal for at least a year, as the era of
border restrictions, snap lockdowns, and economic

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:17.320
uncertainty drags on in the People’s Republic.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:22.380
That’s not the look the country wants both
at home and abroad.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:27.240
Now, none of this is to say that China’s
vaccination practices necessarily are or are

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:32.440
not immoral or harmful or any other value
judgement, but it is to say that the practices

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:35.510
are problematic for China itself.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:40.200
People, both within the country’s borders
are beyond, are going to wonder why doses

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:45.410
are going to foreign arms first, when Chinese
citizens are still vulnerable; they're going

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:50.160
to wonder why China didn't use its newfound
wealth to purchase more effective and faster-delivering

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:54.600
vaccines from foreign manufacturers; they're
going to wonder why, when life is back to

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:59.480
normal in the West, the country that flouts
itself as the conqueror of the Coronavirus

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:02.360
is still far from herd immunity.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:06.670
This wonder will lead to conclusions, and
without the narrative control that they so

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:13.680
desperately work to maintain, China’s foreign
and domestic image might, once again, suffer

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:20.360
in what is, hopefully, COVID-19’s third
and final act.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:26.211
So, $15 is about what it costs to get a fancy
burger, a movie ticket, or a cocktail at a

00:16:26.211 --> 00:16:31.440
nice bar, but it’s also what it costs to
